I can't fall back to sleep I don't even  remember what worked me up to begin with  but now that I'm awake I can't fall back  to sleep no matter how hard I try you  wouldn't even be so bad being awake in  the middle of the night if I could just  get up and move but I can't move a  muscle  I can't even wiggle as much as a toll  and trust me it's not for lack of trying  after the initial panic has set in and  passed and I realized that I wasn't dead  I racked my brain and tried to come up  with an explanation for my immobility I  began to remember a lecture about dreams  and sleep disorders in a psychology  course I took freshman year that's what  made me think of sleep paralysis which  might help explain why the only part of  my body I can move on my eyes may be if  I paid more attention in class I'd be  able to figure out how to raise myself  from this state but as it is I'm stuck  here waiting for one of my roommates to  come check on me in the morning it  doesn't make for much of a plan but it's  all I have it certainly helps stop the  growing pangs of fear that was spreading  through my body although in a pit of my  stomach  I still feel uneasy there is an ominous  yet measured beep that I can faintly  hear too soft to be a fire alarm or a  carbon monoxide detector and it's been  going on for long enough that it's  definitely not a car alarm  it feels both close and distant at the  same time like it's by my side but just  out of reach regardless this isn't the  source of my uneasiness no it's  something else keeping me awake  something else stirring in my chest  giving me a sense of dread it's like  something's in the room with me but I  can't quite see it everything looks a  little blurry like things are moving too  fast there are other sounds like the  soft pitter-patter of feet around me and  just outside my room I can hear what  sounds like whispering since I don't  live alone and the walls are pretty thin  this usually wouldn't be a strange  occurrence even this late at night  however these voices aren't familiar  the murmurs those soft somehow sound  urgent what I want to decipher what  they're saying deep down I know that  even this is not what has me on edge  it's something in the air something is  off as I'm trying to pinpoint what is  making me feel so Restless  the sound of shuffling feet faint  whispers and even the incessant beeping  all began to fade away my vision swims  and darkness begins to swirl around me  growing thicker I can feel my chest  tighten and my breath catch I try to cry  out but no sound emits from my mouth not  a scream nor squeak I tried desperately  to move even an inch but my body doesn't  respond it feels as though I'm being  held down by invisible hands and being  smothered by an infinite darkness and a  deafening silence the pangs of fear that  I suppressed before grow and spread  through my body of a burnin fervor the  uneasiness that world in a pit of my  stomach is now a full-blown terror and  just as I'm about to succumb to my fear  and apparent demise a bright light  parts' the sea of darkness and I'm  brought face to face with a woman the  woman's hair is a ghostly white which  reaches out into the infinite darkness  surrounding her like wispy tendrils her  skin is so pale that it's almost  transparent I feel like I could make out  the bones beneath her skin if I strained  my eyes hard enough but it's not her  hair or her skin that has me captivated  its our eyes or lack thereof well her  eyes are supposed to be  instead I just sunk and black sockets  staring at them I feel as if though I'm  being sucked back into a never-ending  black void with some difficulty I  eventually managed to pull my eyes away  from them looking down I notice that  she's wearing a long white dress that  matches her hair the dress was obviously  once beautiful but now it lies in  tatters clinging to her body like a  vines on a gnarled tree I raise my gaze  to meet hers yet again but before I can  even try to utter a word  she raises a withered finger and points  directly at me  her thin lips part and she'd let sallow  moon as her mouth widens the moon begins  to raise in pitch like a cat will come  in to boil her moon rapidly escalates  into an otherworldly whale her mouth has  now become so impossible wide that its  carnivorous I shut my eyes and covered  my ears in a desperate but futile  attempt to block out the piercing sound  it continues Ford feels like an eternity  I feel blood trickle out of my ears and  down my neck even with my eyes closed I  still see her ghostly [ __ ] looking at  me it feels like she's almost looking  through me directly into my soul when I  finally open my eyes it's not to the  oppressing darkness with the female  Specter or even the familiarity of my  room but to what appears to be the  inside of a hospital room I try to move  and I'm immediately jostled by a sharp  pain in my chest a sharp cry passed my  lips and my hand automatically reached  towards my chest I'm not given much time  to reflect my shock as someone strides  into the room at that moment a pale man  with a bald head looks down at me and  smiles sure enough an impressive set of  white teeth he stressed in a white  overcoat and has a black dress shut  peeking out underneath I wouldn't try to  move if I were you trust me I'm a  professional he says with a mischievous  wink as he steps closer I make out a  name on a badge pinned to his lapel it  reads Dantan with two N's I turned my  head and I'm greeted by a very familiar  beeping the heart monitor is connected  to my chest by tubes and wires I can't  quite see there was also an oxygen mask  lying on my head  the doctor seemingly reads my thoughts  and explains that I had quite a rough  night I was wheeled in by the paramedics  last night after I collapsed in my room  one of my roommates had called 9-1-1 you  had a rather close call he finished  still smiling I begin to straighten up  slightly and he hands me a small cup of  water after a few sips I tell him about  my nightmare he smile never fades as I  talk  sounds like you dreamt of a banshee he  says when I finish he begins to explain  when I give him a quizzical look ghastly  specters to let out blood-curdling cries  they're known as harbingers of death his  grin seems to grow wider as he talks and  I feel an uneasiness sprout in my chest  despite their frightening appearance  there merely warnings that death is  around the corner  I begin to cough and reach for my chest  again death does not like to be cheated  you mortals you build structures and  even create professions just to delay  the inevitable an utterly pointless  venture wouldn't you agree  I clutter up my chest and look back at  the small paper cup of liquid and I  realize it's not water  the man's skin begins to fall away and  he reaches a skeletal finger to pluck  out one of his eyes he removes his white  coat letting it fall to the floor  and pulls up the hood of a black robe  he's wearing the creature looms over me  and gently closes the lids of my eyes I  sincerely hope that your next dream is a  bit more pleasant  [Music]
 

